  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">223609_Start Ready Drought Activation in Zimbabwe (Masvingo)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project seeks to reduce the negative impacts of drought on 4800 households in the targeted area, ward 15, 16, 22, 26, 28, 30 of Masvingo district. The Crop and Livestock Assessment and the ZIMLAC reported that these wards were the most affected and about 44% of the people would need emergency food assistance. This project&apos;s Anticipatory Actions aim to assist these vulnerable households to be better prepared for the drought forecasted by the WFP Standard Precipitation Index. This Anticipatory Actions to be implemented to include promotion of Climate Smart Agriculture practices and crop varieties to reduce crop failure, support livestock production with supplementary feeding and provision of water to reduce mortalities and improve access to early warning weather and climate information for farmers to make informed farming decisions. The project will also promote livelihood diversification so that farmers spread their risk while increasing their income sources. The project will be implemented by World Vision`s local partner, Aquaculture Zimbabwe, working with various relevant stakeholders, departments and line ministries such as Agritex, Veterinary Services Department, Meteorological Services Department, RIDA, Rural District Council, who will provide technical support to the farmers. The project will implement key activities during the November - December 2024 window of opportunity and continue to reinforce and layer the capacity strengthening activities through to October 2025.</narrative>
  </description>
